CLASS com/corrodinggames/rts/game/units/ak com/corrodinggames/rts/game/units/TransportInterface
	METHOD bA isUnloading ()Z
		COMMENT True while this transporter is actively releasing its cargo. Hovercraft stores it in the networked boolean field g (written via writeBoolean/readBoolean for sync), sets it via M() and clears it via ds(); its update loop decrements a timer and pops one unit at a time from getTransportedUnits(), clearing g once the list empties. Consumers: the cancel-unload button (SpecialAction id 110, Hovercraft$2) uses it as both its filter b(Unit) and its enable check, and the unload button's check starts with "!isUnloading()".
	METHOD bB getTransportCapacity ()I
		COMMENT Number of cargo slots this transporter offers. Surfaced to the UI as the unload button's badge/count: Hovercraft$1.b(Unit,boolean) returns it directly, and the button's enable check requires it to be > 0. Implementations return the effective slot count (transportUnitsAddUnloadOption / maxTransportingUnits for CustomUnit, a fixed 12000-style constant for Hovercraft's internal capacity).
	METHOD e removeTransportedUnit (Lcom/corrodinggames/rts/game/units/am;)V
	METHOD f canUnloadNow ()Z
		COMMENT Live "can this transporter release its cargo right now" state. Hovercraft returns !this.cK() (not currently locked/inhibited); CustomUnit returns this.meta.fd.read(this), where the loader sets fd from [core]transportUnitsCanUnloadUnits when present and otherwise from the static fallbacks CustomUnitMetadata.fa / .fb. Consumer: the unload button's enable check, Hovercraft$1.a(Unit,boolean), which reads "!bA() && canUnloadNow() && bB() > 0". Distinct from supportsUnloadAllAction() (j), the static capability flag, and bA(), the "unloading in progress" flag behind the cancel button.
	METHOD j supportsUnloadAllAction ()Z
		COMMENT True when this transporter offers the "unload all" (gui.actions.unload, SpecialAction id 109) button, whose tooltip is "-Will unload all units when stopped". Declared here, implemented by Hovercraft, Dropship and CustomUnit (all return constant true). Its only consumer is the unload button's own per-unit filter: Hovercraft$1.b(Unit) returns ((TransportInterface)am).j(), i.e. the EditorActionButton.b(Unit) "does this action apply to this unit" gate. Distinct from canUnloadTransport() (f), which is the live "can unload right now" state and drives the button's enable check, and from bA(), the "currently unloading" flag behind the cancel button (id 110).
